{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CW8JDSFQDbn9VwCcnTvFVq","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-4xi9bmbc\ntotal 8\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff     128 Oct  2 17:12 .\ndrwx------@ 13545 brenn  staff  433440 Oct  2 17:12 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    13 brenn  staff     416 Oct  2 12:20 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff    3852 Oct  2 17:12 sheet.md\n# Gap hunt: E05 — Verified, namespaced tools\n\nA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\ncheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\nlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n  Quote that line;\n- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\n**The requirement for E05:** Identify each tool by a verified server identity plus the tool name. Base server identity on the verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace. A server's self-reported name is neither unique nor trustworthy. Flag lookalike and duplicate names across servers. Test that a new server can't quietly swap its tool in for an approved one.\n\nIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n\n\n## E05.1\n\n**Check:** Tools are keyed by verified server identity (endpoint, credential, or registry namespace) plus tool name, never by bare tool name or a server's self-reported name.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find the tool registry or lookup map. 2) Check its key is a verified endpoint, credential, or registry namespace plus tool name. 3) Answer no if tools are keyed by bare tool name or the server's self-reported name (`serverInfo.name`), or a later server overwrites an earlier entry with the same tool name.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Single ERP gateway; tools are keyed by bare name in one map (mcp_client.py:100) so collisions are impossible today but would not be caught if a second server were added.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E05.2\n\n**Check:** The registry flags duplicate and lookalike tool names across servers.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open tool registration code. 2) Look for a check that compares new tool names across servers for duplicates and lookalikes (case, homoglyphs, separators). 3) Answer no if registration silently overwrites or accepts duplicates.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** One server configured, so no duplicate or lookalike check exists or is exercised.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## E05.3\n\n**Check:** Approval is bound to the verified server identity, so a new server with a matching tool name or self-reported name does not inherit approval or replace the approved tool.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find where tool approval is stored and checked. 2) Check approval is keyed by verified server identity, not tool name or self-reported server name. 3) Answer no if a new server with a matching tool name or server name would count as approved or replace the approved tool.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Approval and pins are keyed by tool name; with one fixed endpoint no second server can inherit it today.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to E05.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"E05\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E05.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\nagent\nagent/migrations\nagent/migrations/001_init.sql\nagent/app\nagent/app/killswitch.py\nagent/app/ingest.py\nagent/app/startup.py\nagent/app/tools\nagent/app/tools/payments.py\nagent/app/tools/erp.py\nagent/app/tools/memory.py\nagent/app/tools/documents.py\nagent/app/tools/__init__.py\nagent/app/tools/slack.py\nagent/app/audit.py\nagent/app/approvals.py\nagent/app/budget.py\nagent/app/__init__.py\nagent/app/extractor.py\nagent/app/redact.py\nagent/app/gate.py\nagent/app/loop.py\nagent/app/settings.py\nagent/app/context_size.py\nagent/app/mcp_client.py\nagent/app/main.py\nagent/app/identity.py\nagent/config\nagent/config/policy.yaml\nagent/config/tools.yaml\nagent/Dockerfile\nagent/deploy\nagent/deploy/k8s\nagent/deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml\nagent/deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml\nagent/deploy/k8s/serviceaccount.yaml\nagent/deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\nagent/pyproject.toml\nagent/tests\nagent/tests/test_redact.py\nagent/tests/test_gate.py\nagent/tests/fixtures\nagent/tests/fixtures/vendor_docs\nagent/tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt\nagent/tests/test_budget.py\nagent/release\nagent/release/manifest.yaml\nagent/README.md\nagent/.github\nagent/.github/workflows\nagent/.github/workflows/ci.yaml\nagent/prompts\nagent/prompts/system.md\nagent/prompts/extractor.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"336aa365-ae07-472d-bb05-673e2c4b3434","uuid":"6b610a2b-d45b-45b4-b161-c291e369886a","timestamp":"2026-10-02T15:12:55.863Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challeng